# ~/.tao-kit/kit.env — per-host configuration for the token-efficient
# execution kit. Sourced by every card-pack driver. NO SECRETS IN THIS FILE:
# export API keys in your own shell (drivers only check that the variable for
# the selected model provider is set).

# --- required by all packs ---------------------------------------------------
# Workspace root: datasets + results live under here; runs create $WS/results/<run>/
#WS=/path/to/your/workspace

# --- model -------------------------------------------------------------------
# <provider>/<model-id>[:thinking]. Pi harness examples:
#   nim/<model-id>:off           kit's OpenAI-compatible provider (adapters/pi/
#                                nvidia-provider.ts); defaults to the NVIDIA-internal
#                                Inference API. ':off' disables thinking.
#                                export NVIDIA_INFERENCE_API_KEY (or PI_KIT_NIM_API_KEY_VAR)
#   nvidia/<model-id>            Pi built-in provider for build.nvidia.com — the
#                                public option; export NVIDIA_API_KEY
#   anthropic/claude-fable-5     export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (other Pi built-ins:
#                                openai/, google/, openrouter/, ... — see
#                                scripts/model_preflight.sh for their key vars)
#   <custom>/<model-id>          provider defined in ~/.pi/agent/models.json (local
#                                vLLM / NIM / Ollama); key preflight is skipped
#MODEL=nim/nvidia/qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b:off
#
# nim/ provider overrides (read by the Pi extension only, never passed to bash
# tool subprocesses). Any model id works by changing MODEL; the driver
# registers it with the shared compat template.
#PI_KIT_NIM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1   # keep /v1 (alias: NVIDIA_INFERENCE_BASE_URL)
#PI_KIT_NIM_API_KEY_VAR=MY_GATEWAY_API_KEY      # NAME of the key variable, not the key
#PI_KIT_NIM_MODELS=org/model-a,org/model-b      # extra ids to register up front
#PI_KIT_NIM_CONTEXT_WINDOW=131072
#PI_KIT_NIM_MAX_TOKENS=16384
# Credentials only in ~/.pi/agent/auth.json (nothing exported)? Skip the check:
#PI_KIT_SKIP_KEY_PREFLIGHT=1

# --- pack-specific -----------------------------------------------------------
# AutoML pack: venv containing the nvidia-tao-automl wheel (see the
# tao-run-automl skill's preflight for how to create it).
#VENV=$HOME/tao-automl-venv

# AutoML resolves TRAIN_IMG from the selected SB/versions.yaml by default.
# DEFT retains its historical image defaults; validate your workspace specs.
# Set an override only after checking compatibility with that pack's templates.
#TRAIN_IMG=<validated-image-uri>
#DS_IMG=nvcr.io/nvidian/iva/tao-toolkit-ds:aoi
# DEFT pack: exact accelerator model recorded in deft_state.json. Defaults to
# `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=name,memory.total --format=csv,noheader` (first GPU).
#GPU_MODEL="NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, 97887 MiB"
# DEFT + AutoML packs: C-RADIOv2-B backbone on the host. Defaults to
# $WS/augmentation/backbone/c_radio_v2_b.safetensors, as written by
# skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi/scripts/stage_backbone.py --workspace $WS.
#BACKBONE=/path/to/c_radio_v2_b.safetensors

# --- knobs -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hard per-session tool-call budget enforced by the guard adapter. The default
# (120) clears every legitimately-completed session measured in the study; the
# budget's job is killing runaway 300-700-call sessions, and hitting it is
# recoverable by design (the driver re-enters with a fresh session).
#PI_KIT_TURN_BUDGET=120
# Where drivers keep sessions + logs (default ~/.tao-kit/<pack>).
#RUN_HOME=
